<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43764" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Septĭmĭus</span></b> , i,
			m.; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Septĭmĭa</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> C. Septimius, <i>an augur</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				12, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 14,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> P.
			Septimius Scaevola, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 1, 13, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Clu.
				41, 115 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Porcius Septimius, <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			Titius Septimius, <i>a poet and friend of Horace</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 9, 1</span></i> (to him was
			addressed C. 2, 6).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> Septimius Severus, <i>a Roman emperor</i>,
			Spart. Sev.; <i><span class="en">Eutr. 8,
				10</span></i>.—<i>Fem.</i>: Septimia, perh.
				<i>the wife of Sicca</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				16, 11, 1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
